# asahi, hk: Add support for Apple Interchange
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46543 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?
This MR adds support for Apple Interchange, a framebuffer format used for sharing between hardware blocks on Apple SoCs.

It is very similar to the supported AGX tiled and compressed format, however the image tile size is a fixed 16x16 for RGB framebuffers regardless of bit depth. YCbCr formats are the exception, where the tile size is 32x32 for the luma channel and 16x16 for both chroma channels. In all cases, the compression subtiles are 16x16 with 8 bytes of metadata. This is currently unimportant as neither Asahi nor Honeykrisp currently support handling YUV images properly regardless of layout.

AGX itself does not have "full" support for Apple Interchange; tt cannot be used for Z/S buffers or for array textures, for example. We therefore limit its use to single-layer scanout/shared buffers, and only allow it to be used if the corresponding DRM format modifier has been explicitly requested.

No CTS regressions were found on an M2 MacBook Air or M2 Max Mac Studio.
--- include/drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h
+++ include/drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h
@@ -1616,6 +1616,30 @@ drm_fourcc_canonicalize_nvidia_format_mod(__u64 modifier)
 #define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_APPLE_GPU_TILED fourcc_mod_code(APPLE, 1)
 #define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_APPLE_GPU_TILED_COMPRESSED fourcc_mod_code(APPLE, 2)
 
+/*
+ * Apple Interchange layout
+ *
+ * Apple Interchange is a compressed framebuffer format used exclusively for
+ * sharing buffers between hardware blocks (GPU, display controller, video
+ * codecs) on Apple platforms. It is similar to and uses the same compression
+ * scheme as GPU_TILED_COMPRESSED. There is no known uncompressed variant
+ * of Apple Interchange.
+ *
+ * Unlike the GPU layouts, tile size is not dependent on bit depth. RGB
+ * images and the chroma components of YUV images use 16x16 tiles. The
+ * luma component of YUV images uses 32x32 tiles. Compression tiles
+ * are once again 16x16 with 8 bytes of metadata per compression subtile.
+ *
+ * Following the example set by GPU_TILED_{,COMPRESSED}, Interchange images
+ * are treated as a single plane by software and do not have a meaningful
+ * stride.
+ *
+ * AGX has limited support for Apple Interchange. It cannot be used for Z/S
+ * buffers or array images, for example. It is intended for scanout buffer
+ * sharing only.
+ */
+#define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_APPLE_INTERCHANGE fourcc_mod_code(APPLE, 3)
+
 /*
  * AMD modifiers
  *

